<title>POLAND: POLISH UNEMPLOYMENT SEEN AT 11.9 PCT IN '97-REPORT.</title>
<headline>POLISH UNEMPLOYMENT SEEN AT 11.9 PCT IN '97-REPORT.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's unemployment rate could fall to 11.9 percent in 1997, against 13.6 percent last year, Government Centre for Strategic Studies (CSS) said in a report on Wednesday.</p>
<p>CSS said the number of unemployed could fall by 310,000 to 2,050,000 but said the fall would be largely due to the January exclusion of some groups of pensioners and graduates from the official unemployed statistics.</p>
<p>Unemployment in January-April period fell by 228,000 people to 2,132,000.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
